# RUSTSEC-2026-0367 / RUSTSEC-2026-0368 / RUSTSEC-2026-0369: zip extraction
# flaws (SUID/SGID bits preserved, symlink targets escaping the destination,
# Unix permissions applied through symlinks). Patched only in zip >= 9.0.0;
# no 7.x/8.x backport exists (RustSec + OSV both list `fixed = 9.0.0`).
#   https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0367.html
#   https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0368.html
#   https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0369.html
# One copy left in Cargo.lock:
#   zip 7.2.0 <- candle-core 0.10.2 <- finima-embed / mistralrs (optional
#               `candle` features only; not in the default build)
# calamine 0.37 moved finima-ingest (XLS/XLSX/ODS import) to zip 9.x, so the
# default build no longer carries a vulnerable zip.
# Not reachable: all three advisories are in ZipArchive::extract() /
# ZipStreamReader::extract() (writing an archive to the filesystem). candle-core
# only opens the archive and reads entries into memory (ZipArchive::new +
# by_name); it does not call extract(), and finima has no direct zip dependency.
# Why not fixed now: candle-core 0.11.1 (zip ^9.1.3) needs a mistralrs release
# that pins candle ^0.11, and mistralrs 0.8.1 pins candle ^0.10.2.
# Exit: drop once a candle-core on zip >= 9 is in the lockfile
# (`cargo tree -i zip --all-features` shows only 9.x).
RUSTSEC-2026-0367
RUSTSEC-2026-0368
RUSTSEC-2026-0369

